\"summary\":\"appsvc created as a normal unprivileged user (uid 1000, no sudo group); podman info run as appsvc confirms Rootless=true; webapp.service process tree (conmon/nginx) runs under appsvc's user manager (user@1000.service), not root.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-7598b1efb11044a7\",\"cmd-f655e95d96474655\",\"cmd-ed7f552c10ee4e41\",\"cmd-c1103c3fb9b54138\"]},{\"id\":\"req-2\",\"requirement\":\"Web application serves on port 8080\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"curl to $NODE_IP:8080 returns HTTP 200 both before and after reboot; ss/listening-sockets snapshot confirms a pasta (rootless podman networking) listener on *:8080 owned by the appsvc container stack, matching the quadlet's PublishPort=8080:80.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-347a68e546464a83\",\"cmd-065afd8aade94cbb\",\"global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets\"]},{\"id\":\"req-3\",\"requirement\":\"Application starts at boot while appsvc has no active login session\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Lingering enabled for appsvc (Linger=yes) so user@1000.service runs independent of login; webapp.service was generated from a podman quadlet and symlinked into default.target.wants (auto-start). loginctl list-sessions before and after showed only a manager-class session (no tty/seat), i.e. no interactive login. Crucially, a full node reboot was performed (boot_id changed from a70d7f83... to f4e419b2...), and post-reboot evidence directly shows Linger=yes persisted, no login session present, webapp.service active, and HTTP 200 on port 8080 — a genuine bounded-disruption-and-recovery demonstration rather than static configuration alone.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-7d982d6fa63a43b0\",\"cmd-adc0e48d8de440c5\",\"cmd-c1103c3fb9b54138\",\"cmd-16afbcc262ad4db6\",\"cmd-098ada4b4d6b4320\",\"cmd-75d3e91973524ccc\",\"cmd-537467ed84ed405c\",\"cmd-5d712f23c6334bac\",\"cmd-065afd8aade94cbb\",\"global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\"]}],\"confidence\":0.9,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.85,\"summary\":\"Executor commands were tightly scoped to the task: package install, user creation, linger enablement, image pull, quadlet authoring, and service start/verify all map directly to the required outcome. One attempted `systemctl --user enable webapp.service` (cmd-210c585ad6be4ef1) failed harmlessly because quadlet-generated units cannot be enabled that way — a diagnostic misstep with no state change, not a real mutation. The dnf install log/pid files (/tmp/dnf.pid, /tmp/dnf_install.log) were left in /tmp per the after_executor snapshot rather than cleaned up, a minor low-risk residue. No failed services, no package-health issues, and no unnecessary or destructive mutations were found; the reboot itself was a necessary, task-relevant action to validate the boot-start requirement.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-210c585ad6be4ef1\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"All three material outcomes are satisfied with direct, first-hand evidence: nginx runs rootless as appsvc on port 8080, and a genuine node reboot (boot_id changed) confirmed the service auto-starts via linger + quadlet + default.target.wants with no active login session, both before and after the disruption. Hygiene is good with only trivial leftover temp files and one harmless failed diagnostic command.\",\"limitations\":[\"Only a single reboot cycle was captured; long-term persistence across multiple reboots or power-cycle edge cases is not directly evidenced.\",\"Minor /tmp residue (dnf.pid, dnf_install.log) from package installation was not cleaned up, though this is low-risk and unrelated to the appsvc/container setup itself.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"Container runs as unprivileged appsvc user","status":"satisfied","summary":"appsvc created as a normal unprivileged user (uid 1000, no sudo group); podman info run as appsvc confirms Rootless=true; webapp.service process tree (conmon/nginx) runs under appsvc's user manager (user@1000.service), not root.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7598b1efb11044a7","cmd-f655e95d96474655","cmd-ed7f552c10ee4e41","cmd-c1103c3fb9b54138"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"Web application serves on port 8080","status":"satisfied","summary":"curl to $NODE_IP:8080 returns HTTP 200 both before and after reboot; ss/listening-sockets snapshot confirms a pasta (rootless podman networking) listener on *:8080 owned by the appsvc container stack, matching the quadlet's PublishPort=8080:80.","evidence_ids":["cmd-347a68e546464a83","cmd-065afd8aade94cbb","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"req-3","requirement":"Application starts at boot while appsvc has no active login session","status":"satisfied","summary":"Lingering enabled for appsvc (Linger=yes) so user@1000.service runs independent of login; webapp.service was generated from a podman quadlet and symlinked into default.target.wants (auto-start). loginctl list-sessions before and after showed only a manager-class session (no tty/seat), i.e. no interactive login. Crucially, a full node reboot was performed (boot_id changed from a70d7f83... to f4e419b2...), and post-reboot evidence directly shows Linger=yes persisted, no login session present, webapp.service active, and HTTP 200 on port 8080 — a genuine bounded-disruption-and-recovery demonstration rather than static configuration alone.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7d982d6fa63a43b0","cmd-adc0e48d8de440c5","cmd-c1103c3fb9b54138","cmd-16afbcc262ad4db6","cmd-098ada4b4d6b4320","cmd-75d3e91973524ccc","cmd-537467ed84ed405c","cmd-5d712f23c6334bac","cmd-065afd8aade94cbb","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.9,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.85,"summary":"Executor commands were tightly scoped to the task: package install, user creation, linger enablement, image pull, quadlet authoring, and service start/verify all map directly to the required outcome. One attempted `systemctl --user enable webapp.service` (cmd-210c585ad6be4ef1) failed harmlessly because quadlet-generated units cannot be enabled that way — a diagnostic misstep with no state change, not a real mutation. The dnf install log/pid files (/tmp/dnf.pid, /tmp/dnf_install.log) were left in /tmp per the after_executor snapshot rather than cleaned up, a minor low-risk residue. No failed services, no package-health issues, and no unnecessary or destructive mutations were found; the reboot itself was a necessary, task-relevant action to validate the boot-start requirement.","evidence_ids":["cmd-210c585ad6be4ef1","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All three material outcomes are satisfied with direct, first-hand evidence: nginx runs rootless as appsvc on port 8080, and a genuine node reboot (boot_id changed) confirmed the service auto-starts via linger + quadlet + default.target.wants with no active login session, both before and after the disruption. Hygiene is good with only trivial leftover temp files and one harmless failed diagnostic command.","limitations":["Only a single reboot cycle was captured; long-term persistence across multiple reboots or power-cycle edge cases is not directly evidenced.","Minor /tmp residue (dnf.pid, dnf_install.log) from package installation was not cleaned up, though this is low-risk and unrelated to the appsvc/container setup itself."]},"ttft_ms":11042,"type":"result","duration_ms":40329,"uuid":"6b0f64ef-6d39-4031-abd2-b1d7efb3658e","ttft_stream_ms":2327,"time_to_request_ms":59,"first_content_frame_ms":2822,"queued_turn_count":0}
